---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const siteUrl = 'https://nidhi.today';

const profilePageSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'ProfilePage',
  name: 'About nidhi',
  url: `${siteUrl}/about/`,
  description:
    'Who writes nidhi, why the writing can be trusted, and how each post is researched and sourced.',
  // nidhi is the publishing Organization. Using Organization matches the
  // author type on blog posts (changed in commit 41ca037). Inlined here
  // (not a separate JSON-LD document) so Google can resolve the type without
  // cross-document @id references.
  mainEntity: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'nidhi',
    url: `${siteUrl}/about/`,
    description:
      'Practitioner and research-led personal finance education on nidhi.today, covering net worth, multi-currency money management, and financial independence. Builds the tools the posts describe and sources every article against cited references.',
    knowsAbout: [
      'Personal Finance',
      'Financial Literacy',
      'Net Worth Tracking',
      'Multi-Currency Finance',
      'Financial Independence',
      'Money Management',
    ],
    sameAs: ['https://www.instagram.com/nidhi.today'],
  },
};

const breadcrumbSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${siteUrl}/` },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'About', item: `${siteUrl}/about/` },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About nidhi: Who Writes This and Why You Can Trust It | nidhi"
  description="Who writes nidhi, the qualifications behind the writing, and how every personal finance post is researched and sourced."
  jsonLd={[profilePageSchema, breadcrumbSchema]}
>
  <section class="about-page">
    <div class="about-container">
      <div class="about-hero">
        <div class="about-avatar">
          {/* Brand icon mark. Two variants toggled by [data-theme] so the
              avatar follows the manual theme switch, not just the OS
              preference. Rendered at 80px; the 256px source covers DPR 2. */}
          <img
            class="brand-mark brand-mark--light"
            src="/brand/logo/icon-only/icon-256.png"
            width="256"
            height="256"
            alt="nidhi"
            loading="eager"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <img
            class="brand-mark brand-mark--dark"
            src="/brand/logo/icon-only/icon-256-dark.png"
            width="256"
            height="256"
            alt="nidhi"
            loading="eager"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </div>
        <h1 class="about-title">About nidhi</h1>
        <p class="about-intro">
          nidhi is the name on this writing, and the project it belongs to. One person started it, the
          name stuck, and it is who you are reading when you read the blog.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-body">
        <h2>Who is writing</h2>
        <p>
          Every post on this site is written and edited under one name: nidhi. The project began because
          one person could not find a finance tool that handled an ordinary life with money in more than
          one currency, debts in another, and a future that crossed borders. The writing comes from that
          same place: the questions a real person actually has to answer, explained the way they wished
          someone had explained them.
        </p>

        <h2>Why you can trust it</h2>
        <p>
          The authority here is practitioner and research-led, not a wall of letters after a name. nidhi
          builds the tools that the posts describe, which means the writing is grounded in working through
          the numbers, not in repeating talking points. Where a post makes a claim, it points to the
          source: the books, reference pages, and primary material listed on each article under
          "referential reading."
        </p>
        <p>
          What this is not: licensed financial advice. nidhi explains how money works so you can make your
          own decisions. It does not tell you which fund to buy, and it never will. For decisions that turn
          on your specific tax residency, legal situation, or risk tolerance, a qualified professional is
          the right call. That boundary is deliberate, and it is the same one stated in the footer of every
          page.
        </p>

        <h2>How posts are made</h2>
        <p>
          Each article starts from a concrete question, gets worked through with real numbers and worked
          examples, and is checked against cited references before it goes out. The full process, sourcing
          standards, and how corrections are handled live on the
          <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy page</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What nidhi knows about</h2>
        <p>
          The writing concentrates on net worth and how to measure it, managing money across currencies,
          cash flow and saving, debt, and the path to financial independence. If you want the worldview
          behind all of it, read <a href="/beliefs/">our beliefs</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-cta">
        <p class="about-cta-text">Questions, corrections, or just want to say hello?</p>
        <div class="about-cta-links">
          <a href="mailto:hello@nidhi.today" class="about-cta-link" data-attr="about-cta-email">
            Email hello@nidhi.today
          </a>
          <a
            href="https://www.instagram.com/nidhi.today"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="about-cta-link"
            data-attr="about-cta-instagram"
          >
            Instagram @nidhi.today
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: var(--space-10) var(--space-4);
  }

  .about-container {
    max-width: 680px;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .about-hero {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .about-avatar img {
    width: 80px;
    height: auto;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  /* Theme-aware brand mark: show the variant matching the active theme.
     Default (light) shows the light mark; [data-theme="dark"] swaps it. */
  .about-avatar .brand-mark--dark {
    display: none;
  }

  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .about-avatar .brand-mark--light {
    display: none;
  }

  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .about-avatar .brand-mark--dark {
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .about-title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 2rem;
    color: var(--color-deep-blue);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .about-intro {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .about-body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--color-deep-blue);
    margin: var(--space-6) 0 var(--space-2);
  }

  .about-body p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
  }

  .about-body a {
    color: var(--color-teal);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .about-body a:hover {
    color: var(--color-teal-dark);
  }

  .about-cta {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    text-align: center;
    background: var(--color-bg-white);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
  }

  .about-cta-text {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-deep-blue);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .about-cta-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .about-cta-link {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    color: var(--color-deep-blue);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-deep-blue);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: all 0.15s ease;
  }

  .about-cta-link:hover {
    background: var(--color-deep-blue);
    color: white;
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .about-title { font-size: 1.6rem; }
    .about-cta-links { flex-direction: column; align-items: center; }
  }
</style>
